# This module's Go sources are LF in the index and must be LF in the worktree
# too. gofmt compares the bytes ON DISK, so a CRLF checkout makes `gofmt -l`
# list a file that is byte-identical to a clean one — measured: main.go's entire
# gofmt diff was 578 lines of ^M and nothing else. eol=lf overrides
# core.autocrlf=true, which is what put the CRLF there in the first place.
*.go text eol=lf

# The committed CLI binary has no file extension, so git classifies it by
# content sniffing alone (currently -text, correctly). This makes that explicit
# and immune to any future broad rule such as `* text=auto`: the first 12 digits
# of this file's sha256 are the clihash segment of every production cache key
# (b659fff65cb9), and a single converted byte would both corrupt the ELF and
# silently re-key the cache. `binary` is the -text -diff -merge macro; all three
# are correct for a 22MB build artefact.
bin/** binary
